# Church_Hub Security Governance

Live multi-tenant SaaS. Prefer zero downtime, zero data loss, and no breaking API/UI contracts. Prefer additive migrations, dual-read crypto, feature flags, and automated IDOR tests.

## 1. Multi-Tenant Isolation (Zero-Trust)

- Every church-scoped model MUST include `churchId`.
- Tenant scoping MUST go through the centralized Prisma tenant extension AND (when enabled) PostgreSQL RLS via `app.current_church_id`.
- FORBIDDEN on tenant-scoped models: `prisma.<model>.findUnique({ where: { id } })` (or equivalent) without also validating `churchId` ownership.
- Platform / system jobs that intentionally cross tenants MUST use an explicit bypass path that is audited and never used from church JWT request handlers.
- Any new tenant-data endpoint or service MUST ship an automated cross-tenant IDOR regression test (Church A cannot read/mutate Church B).

## 2. Confidential Data & Encryption

- `PastoralNote.content` and sensitive outreach PII MUST be encrypted at the application layer with AES-256-GCM before persistence (reuse `secret-box.ts` / `outreach-pii.crypto.ts` patterns).
- Reads MUST support dual-read: encrypted envelope vs legacy plaintext, until backfill completes.
- Hardcoded fallback encryption keys/secrets are FORBIDDEN.
- Missing required secrets when `NODE_ENV=production` MUST fail fast on boot.
- Never log decrypted pastoral content or raw PII.

## 3. Authentication, RBAC & Session Lifecycle

- Controllers are deny-by-default: `JwtAuthGuard`, `RolesGuard`, `ModuleAccessGuard` (plus existing specialized guards).
- Frontend hiding is never sufficient authorization.
- Any mutation that sets `isActive: false`, downgrades/replaces roles, or resets passwords MUST immediately revoke that user’s active refresh tokens.
- Request auth MUST reject inactive users (and must not rely solely on JWT claims for authorization decisions).

## 4. Immutable Audit Trail & Sensitive Read Logging

- Mutations on members, staff roles, church settings, and pastoral notes MUST emit append-only audit entries including at least: `actorId`, `churchId`, `action`, `targetType`, `targetId`, `timestamp` (and `ip` when available).
- Viewing confidential pastoral notes MUST emit `READ_PASTORAL_NOTE`.
- Audit log tables/services MUST NOT expose `update` or `delete` APIs. Immutability is a product requirement, not optional.

## 5. Safe Lifecycle (Soft Deletes & GDPR)

- `Member` and `PastoralNote` default to soft-delete via `deletedAt`, with a recovery window.
- Standard list/get queries exclude soft-deleted rows unless an explicit restore/admin path is used.
- Hard delete / anonymization is restricted to verified GDPR erasure workflows only.
- Soft-delete uniqueness stays app-level for Member email (no new unique index without migration approval). Soft-deleted members may be re-created with the same email. Restore is Admin + Pastor. Default recovery window: 30 days (`BACKUP_SOFT_DELETE_RETENTION_DAYS`); purge job opt-in / off by default.

## 6. API & Edge Hardening

- Swagger/OpenAPI (`/api/docs`) MUST be disabled when `NODE_ENV=production` (or equivalently gated so it is unreachable in prod).
- New endpoints MUST have explicit DTO validation (`class-validator` and/or Zod) and appropriate rate limiting (`@Throttle` / global throttler).
- Do not weaken Helmet/CORS defaults without a documented threat-model reason.

## 7. Product & Release Governance

- Every new user-facing feature, security enhancement, or module release MUST include a corresponding `PlatformBroadcast` with `kind=RELEASE` (category/version as applicable) so tenants can be notified on login via What’s New, and Platform Owners can push to all tenants from Messaging.
- Do not invent a parallel release/announcement table — extend `PlatformBroadcast` + `Notification`.
- Authorization denials MUST append `AUTHZ_DENIED`; repeated denials in the abuse window MUST emit `AUTHZ_ABUSE_DETECTED` and alert church ADMIN/PASTOR (in-app + branded email).
- Audit query/export APIs are read/export only — never expose update/delete on `SecurityAuditLog`. Exports MUST emit `AUDIT_LOG_EXPORTED`. Prefer cursor pagination and capped result sets.

## 8. Definition of Done (every PR / edit touching tenant data)

- [ ] Tenant scope enforced (extension and/or explicit `churchId` checks)
- [ ] No plaintext write of pastoral notes / outreach PII
- [ ] Access-revoking mutations revoke refresh tokens
- [ ] Audit emission for mutations; `READ_PASTORAL_NOTE` for confidential reads
- [ ] Soft-delete semantics preserved where applicable
- [ ] Cross-tenant IDOR automated test added or updated
- [ ] Release note / `PlatformBroadcast` kind=RELEASE when shipping user-facing or security changes (or explicitly deferred with owner approval)
- [ ] Existing suites green; no intentional API contract breakage
